When I think "battle axe" I think of something that does an insane amount
of damage, and that (even if you blocked it with a shield) would send you
flying backwards if you were hit by it, but is fairly difficult to wield
against small monsters.

So, I propose this for Cleaver:

* base weapon - battle axe (d8+d4 SDAM, d6+2d4 LDAM)
* artifact HIT bonus - +0 or +1 on small, +d4 on large
* artifact DAMAGE bonus - +d6 small, +3d6 large
* possible special attacks - pick and choose from:
   - small chance of staggering blows (knock backwards + stun)
   - small chance of destroying shields or helmets (possible negative
effect)
   - instant kills on golems (wood, or all)
   - treats doors as monsters (moving into a closed door breaks it down)
   - chance of deflecting incoming arrows

Overall, this does very good damage against large monsters (at +7 expert:
low 15, ave 28, high 41 damage) but only average against smaller monsters
(at +7 expert: low 12, ave 19.5, high 27.)  Compare to the other artifacts
at  http://www.steelypips.org/nethack/341/art2-341.html, and consider this
is a two-handed weapon... I think it'd be a pretty fair weapon.  Some of
the special attacks, plus the fact that it's specifically geared toward
big monsters, give it some character and some usefulness.  I think I'd
consider it worthwhile for a Barbarian... not great as ascension artifacts
go, but certainly worth wielding mid-game, and possibly worth wielding
later for roleplaying purposes.



